Before I begin, I would like to say, this game is very ambiguous with its story. One can only grasp at straws in deciphering meaning. There's nothing wrong with that. I mean you could look up the plot online and the theories are just as mindblowing!! (And they would not necessarily be 100% true) Thus, it is very much open ended. So In the end, we are all correct!
(At Least In My Opinion)
Something terrible has happened. You may or not be..... Well, its not good. You must press forward! Believe in your search for familiar faces, that you still have a purpose in Limbo. At the end, perhaps its fate. A blessing in disguise? Perhaps what life has to offer will always be beyond us.
(a) Nothing Is As It Seems;
Minimalistic, but artistic nonetheless. Less is more, as they say...
(b) Rules of the Beyond;
Controls were easy to learn and master.
(c) Riddles;
Can Be thought-provoking. Mostly require timing and a large deal of trial & error. A challenge Is that you try not to look up solutions :P (I dare ya) I just very recently conquered the game cheat-free! (Cue the eyerolls)
(d) Truly Horrific;
Right blend of darkness (in fact 98% of the game), hostility and well mixed sound effects. Arachnophobics and claustrophobics beware!!
(i) Mute Characters;
Whimsical, however it can be tough to dismantle out the story elements.
(ii) Mechanics;
I would say were really few (either jump, grab or push blocks around). Maybe if they were further developed....
(iii) Life's Too Short;
The overall story is minimal. The puzzles are the only thing that buys time (thus the selling point) and once its done stalling. Its over.
8/10

